{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422398-other-barons-of-los-angeles","id":1422398,"title":"Other Barons of Los Angeles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-07T02:10:35-08:00","id":1422398,"title":"Other Barons of Los Angeles","content":"So we know about Nines, Abrams, The Voermans, and Amethyst. Not counting Victor Temple here because he's a PC.<br /> <br /> What other Barons are there? I know there were some mentioned in LA by Night the source book. It would be fair to say that most of the old Barons are no more? Due to the transition from roving gangs to the more stable Council of Barons.<br /> <br /> What are some that would be worth preserving?<br /> <br /> I know I can just make my own Barons and I have done so, Culver City and Inglewood specifically, but having some resources would be beneficial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T02:41:17-08:00","id":1422401,"title":"","content":"Honestly L.A anarch should have evolved into Carthians<br /> <br /> Each Baron being a representative of a part of a city who reunite to choose a president/prince<br /> <br /> Of course democracy in the domain is just an act becuase most barons reached their power by blackmail or coercion and any who disagrees with them is prone to meet final death by the hands of the Brigades of the revolution.<br /> <br /> Propaganda is said all the time but in reality the Anarch Council has a peace treaty with the inner council of the camarilla that has evolved in some form of cold war","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T02:44:53-08:00","id":1422402,"title":"","content":"PD It is presumed that a lot of baron where killed by the Kue Jin or found new domains after running from L.A.<br /> <br /> A lot of vampire problems can be actually solved by running to a smaller cities where there are fewer vampires but enough population to sustain yourself and progeny","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T03:12:16-08:00","id":1422404,"title":"","content":"There are a few mentions of the Sofa Barons, so there are probably a bunch of solo vampires or small coteries who own very small territories in and around LA, who no-one has bothered stomping on (yet).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26420-desparen","name":"Desparen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T06:10:05-08:00","id":1422419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422398-other-barons-of-los-angeles#post1422398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...The Voermans....</div> </div> </div> </div>The Voerman Sister have moved to Vegas, as of information presented in the V5 <i>Anarch </i>book.<br /> <br /> Edit: As far as I know, no other official barons have been named or detailed. And I like to think Disneyland has its own baron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 11-07-2020, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T07:02:20-08:00","id":1422424,"title":"","content":"Disneyland is owned by Pentex, <br /> it's too big a masquerade risk for vamps","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T10:20:41-08:00","id":1422441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422398-other-barons-of-los-angeles?p=1422419#post1422419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Voerman Sister have moved to Vegas, as of information presented in the V5 <i>Anarch </i>book.<br /> <br /> Edit: As far as I know, no other official barons have been named or detailed. And I like to think Disneyland has its own baron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between Core and Anarch I was under the impression that their operations are based out of Santa Monica, but they travel a lot due to their holdings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T10:38:42-08:00","id":1422444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container